date: '2026-11-21'
authors:
- el-oso
why_read: Read this to understand how runtime hardware introspection replaces tens of thousands of lines of handwritten assembly with portable, generic code. You will learn how modern languages can match low-level performance by computing cache block sizes adaptively.
hn_id: '50588696'
comments: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50588696
---

Linear algebra acceleration traditionally relies on massive tables of hand-tuned assembly microkernels tailored to specific CPU models. PureBLAS demonstrates that an adaptive high-level compiler can replace thousands of lines of low-level assembly with portable runtime inspection.

